              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "You mean all this time I'd been drinking this and never knew to all it a Cape Cod??? Oh, well I guess you learn something new every day! At any rate whether you're like me and just call it Cranberry &amp; Vodka or a little more sophisticated and call it a \"Cape Cod\" - Cheers!!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "France C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Whether you call it a Cape Cod, Cape Codder or Vodka Cranberry, this is a pretty simple, yet tasty cocktail. A little strange to state the juice measurement as 1/3 cup - cocktail recipes are usual stated in ounces. I would suggest 1 1/2 ounces vodka + 3 ounces cranberry juice, or even 2 ounces vodka + 4 ounces cranberry. As written, it doesn't make a very full drink, even when filled with ice.",
            "datePublished": "2023-11-12T18:07:10.841Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I like to drink this in the summer in a tall glass, squeezing the lime wedge (or two) into the glass and topping off with club soda. I usually double the alcohol as I like my drinks stronger.",
            "datePublished": "2010-06-08T19:21:38.150Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "rpollardva"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This has been my favorite drink all summer. I usually add a splash of seltzer at the end to fizz it up. Flavored seltzers add new flavor twists. I've even shaken it up with the different flavors of cranberry (cranraspberry is a favorite). Very refreshing during the heat of summer and what better way to get your healthy juices in? :)",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-27T08:02:06.557Z"
          },
          {
